Reaction: $3\,{}^{4}_{2}\text{He} \rightarrow {}^{12}_{6}\text{C} + \gamma\text{ rays}$

$$\begin{aligned}
\text{Mass defect} = \Delta m &= (3\, m_{\text{He}} - m_{\text{C}}) \\
&= (3 \times 4.002603 - 12) = 0.007809\text{ u}
\end{aligned}$$

$$\text{Energy released} = 931\Delta m\text{ MeV} = 7.27\text{ MeV} = 727 \times 10^{-2}\text{ MeV}$$
